# Open-Meteo
// The weather to come, hour by hour, today and tomorrow, for a few cities.
// Every thing it shows is in OpenMeteo.api.spell, as `spell place ingest` wrote it;  each type below adds to its type there,
// with `<extend>`, so looking again at the server never touches a line of this.
// Open-Meteo has no list of forecasts:  each is asked for by a latitude and a longitude, so the page always says both.

an "open meteo page" is a thing
	its "cities" is a list of cities
	its "city" is a city
	to create it
		add a new city with name "Berlin", latitude = 52.52, longitude = 13.41 to its cities
		add a new city with name "New York", latitude = 40.71, longitude = -74.01 to its cities
		add a new city with name "Tokyo", latitude = 35.68, longitude = 139.69 to its cities
		add a new city with name "Buenos Aires", latitude = -34.6, longitude = -58.38 to its cities
		set its city to the first item of its cities
	its "forecasts" is every forecast where its latitude is the latitude of the city and its longitude is the longitude of the city
		// The city's, from Open-Meteo:  asked for by where it is, with no list of them all
	its "forecast" is the first item of its forecasts
		// Its one forecast:  Open-Meteo answers with one, for the nearest place it has

	to draw it
		<stack spacing="xl">
			<stack spacing="sm">
				<header size="large">The weather, from Open-Meteo</header>
				<toolbar appearance="secondary" aria-label="Cities">
					{draw each city in its cities}
				</toolbar>
			</stack>
			{draw the forecast table of it}
			<text size="small" paragraph>
				From <link link="https://open-meteo.com/en/docs">Open-Meteo's API</link>, asked for as you look;  each measure in your own units.
			</text>
		</stack>

	to draw its forecast table
		if its forecast
			<stack spacing="sm">
				<text color="grey">The next two days in {its forecast's timezone}, hour by hour.</text>
				{draw the hour table of its forecast}
			</stack>
		while waiting
			<loader visible inline text>Asking Open-Meteo</loader>
		if that fails
			<text>Open-Meteo can't be reached just now.</text>

# A city
// Where it is on Earth:  what its forecast is asked for by.

a "city" is a thing
	its "name" is text
	its "latitude" is a number
	its "longitude" is a number

	to pick it
		// The city the weather's for
		set the city of the weather of the public servers to it

	to draw it
		<item active={it is the public servers' weather's city} onClick={pick it}>{its name}</item>

# Its hours
// A row an hour:  the day at midnight, the hour, and each measure, in the units the reader's region reads, °F and inches in the US.

a forecast
	to draw its hour table
		for hour in its hours
			<cell "Day"><if the hour of its time is 0>{its time}</if></cell>
			<cell "Hour" align="right">{the hour of its time}:00</cell>
			<cell "Temperature" align="right">{its temperature}</cell>
			<cell "Rain" align="right">{its precipitation}</cell>
			<cell "Wind" align="right">{its wind speed}</cell>
		show them in: <table appearance="very-basic" padding="compact" collapsing unstackable><row></row></table>
